# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1500> (SMN complex)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1500> "The SMN complex is essential for the biogenesis of spliceosomal snRNP particles, which are required for splicing of nuclear pre-mRNAs. Through its binding to specific sequences in the snRNAs, the SMN complex surveys the correct identity of the target RNAs and facilitates snRNP assembly.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1500> "Survival of motor neuron complex")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1500> "SMN complex")
SubClassOf(<https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1500> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0005855>)

# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1504> (Spliceosomal A complex)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1504> "The spliceosomal A complex is an intermediate complex in the assembly of a spliceosome.   The entry of the U2 snRNP to the <a href='https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1522'>E complex</a> defines the branch-point and leads to the formation of the A complex. The A complex associates with the <a href='https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1506'>U4/U6.U5 tri-snRNP</a> to generate the <a href='https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1507'>B complex</a>.   ")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1504> "PS complex")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1504> "prespliceosome complex")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1504> "Spliceosomal A complex")
SubClassOf(<https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1504> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0005855>)

# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1534> (Mitochondrial RNase P complex)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1534> "Metazoans have two RNase P enzymes: a nuclear RNA-based RNase P and a mitochondrial PRORP (protein-only RNase P). Human mitochondrial RNase P consists of three subunits and lacks an RNA component. RNase P enzymes are metal ion-dependent endonucleases: hydrolases that catalyze site-specific phosphodiester bond hydrolysis primarily within pre-tRNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1534> "mitochondrial PRORP")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1534> "mt-RNase P complex")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1534> "protein only RNase P")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1534> "proteinaceous RNase P")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1534> "Mitochondrial RNase P complex")
SubClassOf(<https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1534> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0005855>)

