AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1855> "Nectins and Nectin-like molecules (Necl) are families of cellular adhesion molecules involved in Ca2+-independent cellular adhesion.Nectins are ubiquitously expressed and have adhesive roles in a wide range of tissues such as the adherens junction of epithelia or the chemical synapse of the neuronal tissue.")
