AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/2141> "Bridge-like lipid transporter proteins are key regulators of intraorganellar lipid trafficking. The BLTP proteins form physical bridges that span the gap between a donor and a receiver organelle and are are formed by multiple repeats of one motif: a repeating beta groove (RBG), which forms an extremely long semi-open tube with a hydrophobic interior.")
